**#7597 is back in the queue.** The reviewer confirmed the rework: the only change is removing the assertion, while the fail-closed branch stays. It agreed with the broader point: an assertion on pack content was a wrong assumption, not an invariant. The new head clears the rejection by itself, so I did not merge master.

D2 is stacked on #7597's old head, so I told the C# session to merge the new head (`5c4ace9d56`) before marking D2 ready, and to drop the same assertion if it copied it into its per-group recomputation. My own PR A lane will pick up the new head when it merges D2. I also added a note to memory: never assert on pack content, not even in debug builds.

