D2 merged #7597's new head cleanly. It calls the Go promotion function directly, so it inherits the fail-closed version, and nothing it measured depended on the old assertion.

D2 adds one `debug_assert!` of its own, a group-backing check. I asked the C# session to confirm that pack content can't reach it. If it is purely an internal invariant of D2's grouping code, it can stay. If conflicting or partial pack data could violate it, it should become a fail-closed Unknown or Ambiguous answer, so it doesn't hit the same queue rejection #7597 did.

