The group-backing assertion already exists on master; D2 only moved one call. It requires every pack behind one alias group to share the same backing, either decoded packs or catalog rows. The C# session thinks pack data could reach it only through a symbol whose language differs from its manifest's, or through one language with mixed backings. Its lane is checking per-symbol language validation, mixed-backing paths and existing fixtures. If external data can reach the assertion, D2 will fail closed instead. The answer comes with D2's final head.

