The C# session found a real bug through that assertion. Grouping by owner ID reads members from every active pack regardless of language. So a valid Rust pack and Go pack that happen to share an owner ID put a Go member into a Rust group. Debug builds trip the assertion, and every build gives the Rust answer a foreign member. The bug has been on master since an earlier change. The fix (reads for one group come only from packs of that group's language) goes into D1, and D2 inherits it.

I confirmed no Go path legitimately spans languages in one group. Go pack symbols are produced and tagged as Go, and the Go promotion code already filters on language, so the language-scoped read is right for Go. I'll check the Go side of it when D2's final head arrives.

