The #7617 lane finished the capability change. Java and Go now both opt into direct type shapes, other languages stay unchanged, and three Go golden rows moved, each audited. All checks passed except the pack drift check, which hit a known line-ending false positive.

It stopped on one question: the store's shape renderer is JVM-specific, so it couldn't add a Go golden without a new test API. I decided against adding one. The regression goes at the Go native-points boundary, through the same public request the sanitizer bridge and the #7616 test use. It asserts structured `Slice` and `Map` forms, plus today's honest results for function types (no shape) and channels (unsupported). The lane is also rerunning the drift check with the line-ending override.

