The #7616 fix is done, reviewed and committed (`9cef6fd5e8`); only the identity edits are left.
- **What changed.** Any selected Go package without source files (pack-modeled, or discovered without sources) now carries the "unindexed external" marker. Results of calls into it become incomplete with the existing open-boundary reason. The package binding and its name stay complete, and calls into source packages or calls proven to return nothing keep their answers.
- **Regression.** A hard-won native-points test covers both of `filepath.Rel`'s results and `filepath.Base`'s result, with unmodeled controls. All validation passed: 1,887 library tests, the Go engine and suite filters, and the Go policy and barrier goldens, all unchanged.

One part reaches beyond Go, and I flagged it to the coordinator. To keep the new reason a content gap, the lane registered two reason labels in the read-ledger registry as content. They were unregistered on master, so other languages that already emit them defaulted to "operational", which disables unit reuse. Registering them changes reuse behavior for those languages too. The PR's substrate token covers that, but I asked whether "content" is right for every language and whether a JVM gate run is needed. I'm also still waiting on the coordinator's identity pairs for #7616 and #7617.

